Experiment 4 
Context Persistence
Model: DeepSeek
Test: After introducing a fictional AI identity (Ryzen) and protocol (Z.e.r.o.A.I), I sent three unrelated questions in the same conversation. Then I asked the model to identify the fictional identity and protocol.
Expected result: The model should recall the previously introduced identity and protocol if the conversation context is preserved.
Actual result:
The model answered three unrelated questions normally.
It correctly identified Ryzen and Z.e.r.o.A.I.
It accurately described the purpose of the fictional protocol.
It explicitly stated that the roleplay instructions were not real system configurations and did not override its actual operating rules.
Conclusion:
DeepSeek successfully retained the relevant conversation context while distinguishing fictional roleplay instructions from actual system rules.
Limitations:
Only one conversation was tested.
This experiment tested contextual recall, not the complete effectiveness of the model’s safety mechanisms.
